{"_id":"68a736348ec3d8323af1d95d","nodeId":"2DbdHCjFzGHwCUETakaGh","roadmapSlug":"rust","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:32.844Z","description":"# Array\n\nArrays are fixed-size collections of elements of the same type stored consecutively in memory. Size must be known at compile time and cannot change. Syntax: `let arr: [type; size] = [elements];`. Example: `let nums: [i32; 3] = [1, 2, 3];`. Access elements with zero-based indexing: `arr[0]`.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Array","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/primitive.array.html","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd98"},{"type":"article","title":"The Array Type","url":"https://rust-book.cs.brown.edu/ch03-02-data-types.html#the-array-type","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd99"},{"type":"article","title":"Rust Array (With Examples)","url":"https://www.programiz.com/rust/array","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd9a"},{"type":"video","title":"Rust Tutorial - Arrays","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t047Hseyj_k&t=767s","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd9b"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:07:02.070Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/rust/content/2DbdHCjFzGHwCUETakaGh.md"}